===BODY===
          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>First, get the car somewhere safe.</strong> After a breakdown or accident abroad, the car is usually taken to a local garage or pound first. On French motorways, for example, only the official breakdown operator may tow you off the motorway, so that part is always done locally.</li>
            <li><strong>Contact us.</strong> Tell us where the car is (the garage name and address if you have it), the make and model, whether it rolls and steers, and where it needs to go in the UK.</li>
            <li><strong>Get a fixed price.</strong> We quote a fixed price for the whole journey, door to door, before anything is booked.</li>
            <li><strong>We bring it home.</strong> Your vehicle is collected on a transporter, brought across the Channel by ferry or the Eurotunnel, and delivered to your home, your own garage or a dealer of your choice.</li>
          </ol>

          <h2>What we need from you</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>The address where the vehicle is now, and a contact there (garage, pound or hotel).</li>
            <li>The keys, or confirmation that they're with the garage.</li>
            <li>Your V5C logbook details, so we can show the vehicle is yours.</li>
            <li>A note telling the garage it may release the car to us, and any garage or storage fees settled.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Insurance and European breakdown cover</h2>
          <p>Many European breakdown policies include repatriation of the vehicle if it can't be repaired within a set number of days. Check your policy or call your insurer first. If you're not covered, or your insurer asks you to arrange it yourself, we'll give you a written quote you can send on to them.</p>

          <h2>Cars bought abroad, too</h2>
          <p>Bought a car in Europe, or moving back to the UK? We also transport running and non-running vehicles from the continent to the UK. The import and registration paperwork is your responsibility, but we take care of getting the car here.</p>

